# ==============================================================================
# ZERACLE TESTNET DEPLOYMENT CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================
#
#   *** LOUD WARNING ***
#   Copy this file to `deployments/testnet/.env` and fill in real values.
#   NEVER commit `.env` and NEVER ship it in a release tarball — see
#   devops/production/ec2/scripts/make-release-tarball.sh's exclude list.
#   DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY below controls REAL Sepolia ETH. A leaked key means
#   real funds stolen. Treat this file like a password vault entry.
#
#   A SECOND secret file lives alongside this one:
#   `deployments/testnet/deployer-account.json` — the L2 deployer's own
#   secretKey/salt/signingKey, generated automatically by deploy-testnet.sh
#   (via DEPLOYER_ACCOUNT_FILE, read by v1-l2/scripts/deploy.ts) on the
#   first run and reused on every re-run so the deployer address doesn't
#   change mid-pipeline. It is NOT set here — there's nothing to fill in —
#   it's created for you and chmod'd 600. Same rules apply: BACK IT UP right
#   after it's created, NEVER commit it, NEVER ship it in a release tarball
#   (already excluded in make-release-tarball.sh alongside this file).
#
#   A THIRD secret file, same treatment: `deployments/testnet/
#   fee-custodian-account.json` — the D-b fee custodian's OWN secretKey/
#   salt/signingKey (Db-4), distinct from the deployer's. deploy-testnet.sh
#   sets FEE_CUSTODIAN_ACCOUNT_FILE to that path and exports it before
#   calling `yarn deploy:clean`, which now REQUIRES the var in testnet mode
#   (deploy.ts refuses to run without it) and creates the file, chmod'd 600,
#   on first run. Not set here either — nothing to fill in. Splitting the
#   custodian's key out from the deployer's means the keeper that later
#   sweeps fees as the custodian (deployments/lib/keeper/run-keeper.sh) never
#   needs the deployer's L2 secret. The custodian needs NO on-chain
#   deployment: like the deployer it is an initializerless account, so
#   sweep-fees.ts sends from it directly and pays through the sponsored
#   FPC. BACK IT UP right after it's created,
#   NEVER commit it, NEVER ship it in a release tarball — excluded in
#   devops/production/ec2/scripts/make-release-tarball.sh (Db-R16), next
#   to the deployer-account.json exclude.
#
#   "Testnet" here means the OFFICIAL Aztec testnet (real sequencing,
#   proving, fee infrastructure) plus Sepolia for L1 — never the sandbox.
#   Sepolia chain id is 11155111. The local sandbox L1 (31337) must NEVER
#   appear as TESTNET_L1_RPC_URL; deploy-testnet.sh's preflight guards this.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Required ---

# Sepolia L1 RPC endpoint (Alchemy/Infura/etc — must resolve to chain id
# 11155111). deploy-testnet.sh's preflight calls `cast chain-id` against this
# URL and aborts if it doesn't answer exactly 11155111.
TESTNET_L1_RPC_URL=

# Deployer's L1 private key (0x-prefixed, 32-byte hex). This account pays
# gas for every L1 contract deploy (mock tokens/feeds, TokenPortal bridge)
# and bridges fee-juice for the L2 deploy. MUST be funded with real Sepolia
# ETH ahead of time (get some from a Sepolia faucet). NEVER the anvil dev
# key here — that key is public and only valid for local sandbox use.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# URL of an Aztec node/sequencer already running on the OFFICIAL Aztec
# testnet (not a local sandbox PXE). Used to fetch L1 contract addresses
# (Inbox/Rollup/Registry/FeeJuicePortal) via getNodeInfo and to bridge
# fee-juice for the L2 deploy. Ask the Aztec testnet operators / docs for a
# current endpoint.
# Published in the public manifest chain-view loads (endpoints.aztecNode) —
# same rule as PUBLIC_L1_RPC below: it must NOT carry credentials (no userinfo,
# no long opaque provider-key path segment, no key/token/auth/secret query
# param). The preflight refuses it otherwise, before anything is broadcast.
AZTEC_NODE_URL=

# Public read RPC for Sepolia that chain-view embeds in the browser: an unkeyed
# endpoint, or a provider key restricted to the dashboard's origin. NEVER reuse
# TESTNET_L1_RPC_URL here. Required: the public manifest refuses keyed URLs.
PUBLIC_L1_RPC=

# --- Optional ---

# Minimum deployer L1 ETH balance (in ether) required to proceed past
# preflight. Default 0.5 — enough headroom for L1 deploys + bridge wiring
# + L2 fee-juice bootstrap. Raise if gas prices spike.
MIN_DEPLOYER_BALANCE_ETH=0.5

# Set to 1 to skip the interactive "Type 'deploy' to continue" confirmation
# prompt after preflight (e.g. for CI/scripted runs). Leave unset for
# interactive use — this is a real-money deploy, the prompt is a safety net.
SKIP_CONFIRM=

# Etherscan API key. Optional — when set, the L1 forge targets (deploy-
# testnet-l1, deploy-mocks-testnet, deploy-bridge-testnet, deploy-governance-
# testnet) run with --verify so the deployed contracts are source-verified on
# Etherscan (Sepolia). Leave unset to deploy unverified; the preflight prints
# whether it detected a value either way. Get one from
# https://etherscan.io/myapikey.
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# T5: the L2 deploy's sandbox-only fee-juice faucet mint is unavailable on
# the official testnet (no free-mint path on a real network). Instead,
# v1-l2/scripts/deploy.ts bridges the deployer's OWN L1 fee-asset balance
# (the L1 fee-juice token the Aztec node reports) non-mint. deploy-testnet.sh
# checks that balance in its Stage 0 preflight, before any Sepolia broadcast,
# and fails loud if the deployer is short; deploy.ts repeats the check right
# before its bridge as a second guard. See L1_FEE_ASSET_BRIDGE_AMOUNT below
# to size that bridge; DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY above must already hold at least
# that much of the L1 fee-asset token.
#
# ZER-28 (T7) — USER fees on testnet go through Aztec's CANONICAL SponsoredFPC.
# Every L2 transaction the web app sends for an end user (transfers, deposits,
# withdrawals, escrow, and since aztec 5.2.0 the in-browser account deploy) is
# paid by a SponsoredFPC. On testnet that is Aztec's own canonical instance,
# which Aztec deploys AND funds. Zeracle deploys no SponsoredFPC on testnet and
# there is no funding step to run: `yarn fund:fpc` and the chain-view admin
# panel are both sandbox-only, so a Zeracle-owned instance here could never be
# topped up. deploy.ts DERIVES the canonical address from SPONSORED_FPC_SALT
# (@aztec/constants) — the same salt Aztec's own deploy uses — so it tracks
# Aztec's deployment rather than a hard-coded literal that could drift. It is
# not configured here, and nothing needs to be pasted below.
#
# Note this is separate from the DEPLOYER's own gas, covered above: the
# deployer still bridges its own L1 fee-asset balance for its deploy
# transactions. CANONICAL_SPONSORED_FPC_ADDRESS below remains an UNUSED
# placeholder for routing that DEPLOYER gas through the canonical FPC too — a
# different design that was not chosen. Nothing reads it; left here in case
# that direction is revisited later.
CANONICAL_SPONSORED_FPC_ADDRESS=

# T5: base-10 integer, base units of the L1 fee-asset token (same decimals as
# Aztec's fee-juice ERC20) to bridge non-mint for the deployer's own L2 gas.
# The deployer's L1 EOA (DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY above) must already hold at
# least this much — there is no testnet faucet. deploy-testnet.sh's Stage 0
# preflight (which also runs under --preflight-only) fails loud before any
# Sepolia broadcast if the balance is short. Optional; defaults to
# one whole token (10^18 base units) if unset.
#
# ZER-11 — WHERE THE 10^18 DEFAULT COMES FROM, AND WHAT IT IS NOT:
#   Measured (Phase 2 rehearsal, batch-C-report.md "Deployer fee spend"):
#     SponsoredFPC deploy ...... 12805894614629      (~1.28e13)
#     whole L2 deploy .......... 162039472016017     (~1.62e14)
#   The 10^18 default is therefore about 6,171x the measured whole-deploy
#   spend. That measurement was taken in testnet MODE but at SANDBOX FEE
#   LEVELS (the rehearsal forced testnet mode against a local node), so it is
#   a LOWER BOUND ONLY. It has NOT been validated against real Sepolia /
#   Aztec-testnet fee levels, and no live deploy has ever been run.
#   The margin is the safety factor, not the measurement.
#
#   Raise this if a real testnet fee market turns out to price the deploy
#   above one token. The asymmetry favours erring high, but be clear about
#   what "high" costs: whatever is bridged and not spent stays as the
#   deployer's L2 fee-juice balance, usable only as future gas on that one
#   account. There is no withdraw path back to L1 in this codebase, so it is
#   not recovered as value. Running dry is worse, though: it strands the
#   deploy mid-flight, after Stage 1 has already paid for every L1
#   transaction.
#
# Left commented out below: an uncommented empty value would still be
# exported (deploy-testnet.sh sources .env with `set -a`), but
# resolveFeeAssetBridgeMode() treats an empty string as unset either way, so
# this is belt-and-braces, not load-bearing.
# L1_FEE_ASSET_BRIDGE_AMOUNT=

# Governance (G3). GOV_PROPOSER is REQUIRED: the Safe that proposes in phase 2; must be a
# deployed contract and must differ from the deployer. Defaults: 180 d transition, 48 h delay.
# NOTE: sandbox-local/deploy-sandbox.sh defaults GOV_PROPOSER/GOV_GUARDIAN to well-known anvil
# dev accounts (#2/#3) for local convenience — those defaults are sandbox-only and are NEVER
# used here; both are REQUIRED below with no default.
GOV_PROPOSER=

# D1: REQUIRED break-glass second proposer — a cold EOA or second Safe, so
# loss of the primary Safe (GOV_PROPOSER) cannot freeze governance after the
# transition. Must differ from both the deployer and GOV_PROPOSER. No code
# check — an EOA is expected here, unlike GOV_PROPOSER.
GOV_PROPOSER_2=

# D2: GOV_GUARDIAN is REQUIRED and must be a separate key from the deployer
# (no default here — see the sandbox note above).
GOV_GUARDIAN=

GOV_TRANSITION_SECONDS=15552000
GOV_TIMELOCK_DELAY=172800

# D5: resumable deploy. Optional — leave all three unset for a fresh
# governance deploy. If set, ALL THREE must be set together, and each must
# already have code on Sepolia; deploy-testnet.sh then reuses them instead
# of deploying a new GovernanceAuthority/ZeracleTimelock/UpgradeValidator.
# GOV_AUTHORITY=
# GOV_TIMELOCK=
# GOV_VALIDATOR=
